@page "/wiki/planets"
@page "/wiki/planets/{Key}"

@*
    The worlds, which are the one shelf where the artwork is the entry.

    Sixty-nine of them and not one description: the game writes no pc_ocean_desc anywhere, so what a
    world has to say is said by the habitability trait an empire evolving there would carry. That is
    borrowed here, exactly as the designer's own picker borrows it.

    The second address is one entry of the shelf. It shows the same page and picks that one out, so a
    reader who found the thing they came for can send somebody straight to it rather than to a list
    with an instruction to scroll.
*@

<PageTitle>Planets - Stellaris Empire Manager</PageTitle>

<WikiSection Kind="WikiKind.Planets" Focus="@Key" />

@code {
    /// <summary>The entry the address names, where it names one.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Key { get; set; }
}
